==Solution 5 ==
Let the point of intersection of <imath>AB</imath> and the kite with <imath>A</imath> as vertex be <imath>D</imath>. 

Let the left kite with <imath>C</imath> as a vertex touch the kite with <imath>A</imath> as vertex at point <imath>E</imath>. 

<imath>\triangle ADE</imath> is a <imath>30-60-90</imath> so <imath>AD = \frac{3}{2}</imath> and <imath>DE = \frac{\sqrt3}{2}</imath>.

So, <imath>AB = 4\cdot AD = 6</imath> and <imath>CD=CE+DE= \frac{3\sqrt3}{2}</imath>, and the area is <imath>\frac12\cdot AB \cdot CD = \boxed{  \textbf{(B) } \frac{9}{2} \sqrt3}.</imath> 

