The figure made of kites was in fact, an einstein tile (also known as the Hat). The einstein tile was discovered in November of 2022 by a retired printing systems engineer in England. It comes from the German word for one stone, and has been proven to infinitely tile a plane aperiodically, quite a unique property - it took decades for mathematicians to find a periodical tilings of smaller and smaller numbers, with Penrose discovering a method using only 2 tilings in 1974.
